  "event:evt.gen_17.circumcision_command": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-chronologist@5",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T13:51:57+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "The command of circumcision (17:9-14) is carried out at 17:23-27 'as God had said'. Linked with TRIGGERS rather than FULFILLS_PROPHECY because it is a command, not a prediction; the text itself says Abraham acted because God had spoken."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:53:31+00:00",
     "note": null,
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    }
   ],
   "source": null
  },
  "event:evt.gen_17.circumcision_performed": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-chronologist@5",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T13:51:57+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "'In the selfsame day' (17:23, 26) is anchored on the end of the ascension, with a margin of a few hours. Rashi, Radak and Sforno read it as the very day of the command, by day and not by night. The duration of about 4 hours is an estimate for 318+ household males (Ibn Ezra on 17:26: 318 born in the house); Ramban/Radak say Abraham circumcised the others first and himself last."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:53:31+00:00",
     "note": null,
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    }
   ],
   "source": null
  },
