  "event:evt.gen_17.el_shaddai_appears": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-chronologist@5",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T13:51:57+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "Dated by the stated age (99), offset 99 years from anchor.abraham_birth, margin 1 year. Cross-check: Ishmael was born when Abram was 86 (evt.gen_16.ishmael_born, c. 2080 BCE) and was 13 at the circumcision (17:25), which gives the same 99. Radak (17:1) says the revelation came 13 years after Ishmael's birth, and Radak on 17:24 places it at the end of Abram's 99th year, a year before Isaac (17:21, 21:5 at 100). The date therefore falls in the last part of year 99; the margin of 1 year covers this but is not shifted.",
    "Divine speeches checked: the multiplication and land promises (17:2-8) are not fulfilled within this chapter (Ishmael's twelve princes, Gen 25; the land, later books); the name changes (17:5, 15) are acted on only later in the text. No in-chapter fulfilment link is therefore written besides the circumcision."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:53:31+00:00",
     "note": "[consider] If the corpus convention allows, use an offset of 99.5 years with a margin of 0.5 years so that the window is exactly the 99th year of life. (GEN.17.1: \"Abram was ninety years old and nine\"; GEN.17.21: \"at this set time in the next year\" (Isaac born at 100, Gen 21:5))",
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    }
   ],
   "source": null
  },
  "event:evt.gen_17.isaac_and_ishmael_promised": {
   "status": "approved",
